      "writtenOn": "2025-01-27T21:52:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two layers today:\n\nFramework: default comes from sysprop `dalvik.vm.madvise.artfile.size` (currently set to UINT_MAX via `runtime_libart.mk`, which is inherited for basically every device). This is fed to ART as a runtime arg. \nART: default comes from `runtime_options.def` (currently set to 0) if nothing passed from the framework.\n\nBecause the framework always sets `dalvik.vm.madvise.artfile.size` via `runtime_libart.mk`, the global default is effectively always `UINT_MAX`. \n\nWith this topic, I moved the framework default from `runtime_libart.mk` into `AndroidRuntime.cpp`. With the flag enabled, we suppress that UINT_MAX default, deferring to ART where the default is 0 (disabled).\n\nIt\u0027s a bit convoluted, but I wanted to do this with a rampable aconfig flag. The alternative would be to just have a rampable mainline ART aconfig flag to simply ignore/disable the madvise entirely. I messaged @ngeoffray@google.com earlier about which he prefers, I don\u0027t feel strongly.",
      "parentUuid": "3ba57e3c_0382e2f5",
      "revId": "50d286a4eaf33925c40ce7610f255108441e6b01",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
